<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28633" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnander</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnandros</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> ; Gr. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen.</i> Menandru, acc. to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μενάνδρου</span>, Ter. Eun., Heaut., and Ad.),
			i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μένανδρος</span>, <i>a celebrated Greek comic
				poet, whom Terence took as his model</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fin. 1,
				2, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ter. And. prol. 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 3,
				21, 28</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nobilis comoediis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 5, 1, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Amm. 21, 4, 4</span></i>.—Form
			Menandros, <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 1, 15, 18</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also Menandrus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vell.
					1, 16, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A slave of Cicero</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				16, 13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A freedman of T. Ampius Balbus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				13, 70</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnandrēus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the
				poet Menander, Menandrian</i>, <i><span class="en">Prop. 2,
			5</span></i> (6), 3.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnandrĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fluxus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pall. 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
